# Vydon Mockery Rules

## Use `.EXPECT()` exclusively

- Mockery exposes two syntaxes: `.On("MyFunction", ...)` (string-based) and `.EXPECT().MyFunction(...)` (type-safe).
- Always use `.EXPECT()`. The string form silently breaks when signatures change.

### Bad

```go
encryptor := sym_encrypt.NewMockInterface(t)
encryptor.On("Encrypt", mock.Anything).Return("token", nil).Once()
```

### Good

```go
encryptor := sym_encrypt.NewMockInterface(t)
encryptor.EXPECT().Encrypt(mock.Anything).Return("token", nil).Once()
```

## Always declare call counts

- Append `.Once()`, `.Twice()`, `.Times(n)`, or `.Maybe()` to every expectation.
- A missing count masks regressions where a mock is invoked more (or fewer) times than expected.

## Mock construction

- Construct mocks with `NewMock<Iface>(t)` so the testify cleanup runs automatically.
- Do not stub return values inline at construction time; assign them per sub-test for clarity.

## Mock file location

- Generated mocks live next to the interface source as `mock_<InterfaceName>.go`.
- Never edit a `mock_*.go` file by hand. Re-run `mockery` after interface changes.
